# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Unsloth's llama.cpp on CUDA, the tree both Qwen models run on and share one build dir for:
# sourced by models/qwen36-35b.env (on CUDA) and models/qwen38-flash.env, so the pin moves for both
# at once. Not a model: models/trees/ is outside the models/*.env the model list reads.
#
# The tree Unsloth Studio ships, built here from its source. Its sparse attention runs a banded
# flash-attention kernel (FLASH_ATTN_EXT_BANDED); mainline 8212c78 and master of 2026-09-29 run
# Qwen3.8-Flash's dense over a full mask, which needs VRAM at runtime the buffers leave no room for:
# it died at ~2.5k tokens of prefill twice. For Qwen3.6 it measured equal to mainline to 0.5 %, the
# same drafts accepted, the same VRAM (T-038). The source commit is not fetchable from the repo, so
# the pin is the release tarball Studio's prebuilt b11160 was built from, with its checksum.
# See docs/qwen36.md#one-tree-for-both-qwen-models.
: "${LLAMA_REPO:=https://github.com/unslothai/llama.cpp}"
: "${LLAMA_COMMIT:=a3c12db9dfc9a5bdf93df199ec370e9faf117c69}"
: "${LLAMA_TARBALL:=$LLAMA_REPO/releases/download/b11160-mix-a6922cc/llama.cpp-source-commit-$LLAMA_COMMIT.tar.gz}"
: "${LLAMA_TARBALL_SHA256:=cbd0e8c756da5b2f46df4ddacded46c7733316c44d86a1a5d176fe3ade7b0675}"
: "${LLAMA_DIR:=$QWEN_HOME/llama.cpp-unsloth}"
# CCCL 3.2, fetched by cmake from NVIDIA's repo at tag v3.2.0, instead of the toolkit's (12.9 ships
# 2.8): the sparse attention's top-k then runs cub::DeviceTopK. Without it the fallback sorts every
# indexer row with temporaries of [depth x ubatch] from the CUDA pool, which grows past the card at
# 19k of context on a fresh prompt and at ~48k in an agent session (T-049). Costs Qwen3.6 nothing.
: "${LLAMA_CMAKE_ARGS:=-DGGML_CUDA_CUB_3DOT2=ON}"
PATCH_DIR=""
